ROUTE CONTRACTS (all POST, JSON; container base http://<name>:8000):

1) payment-processor-sim  POST /v1/charge
   req  {transaction_id:str, amount:float, currency:str, route:str, trace_id?:str}
   resp {status:'CAPTURED'|'DECLINED', processor:str, auth_code:str|null, latency_ms:int}
   Driven by Settings.sim_approval_rate / sim_latency_ms / sim_failure_mode. sim_failure_mode in {none,timeout,error}: non-'none' -> HTTP 503 (detail 'processor failure: <mode>') so routing/decision can fail over (docs/06 §5). simulate_charge(route, settings, rng) in sim.py is pure + seedable (inject random.Random for determinism). Settings fields use ENV ALIASES (SIM_APPROVAL_RATE etc.) with NO populate_by_name, so to override in tests construct Settings(**{'SIM_APPROVAL_RATE':...}) with UPPER-CASE alias keys, not snake_case.

2) ml-scoring-service  POST /v1/score
   req  {model:'risk'|'fraud', model_version:str='latest', features:dict[str,float], metadata:dict}
   resp {score:float, model:str, model_version:str, top_features:[{name:str, contribution:float}], latency_ms:int}
   Loads artifacts at startup (FastAPI lifespan) via <ML_MODELS_DIR>/model_card.json: models.risk.artifact (XGBoost .json via Booster.load_model) + models.fraud.artifact (LightGBM .txt via lightgbm.Booster(model_file=...)); NEVER hardcodes the 2026 date. GET /readyz -> 'loading' until lifespan loads, then 'ready' (artifacts loaded) or 'ready-degraded' (heuristic). If card/artifact absent or load fails -> deterministic heuristic (heuristic.py), model_version='heuristic-v1', bounded score in [0,1], logs degraded notice. Feature vector ordered by acip_common.features.FEATURE_COLUMNS; top_features from pred_contribs (xgb)/pred_contrib (lgbm). ScoreRequest/Response set ConfigDict(protected_namespaces=()) because fields are named 'model'/'model_version'. Pinned xgboost==2.1.3, lightgbm==4.5.0, numpy==2.1.3 (match ml/pyproject.toml). Dockerfile installs libgomp1 (LightGBM runtime). ENV ML_MODELS_DIR defaults to /app/ml/models (compose FEAT-004 mounts ml/models read-only there).

3) llm-gateway  POST /v1/complete
   req  {system:str, prompt:str, temperature:float=0.2, max_tokens:int=512, response_schema?:dict|null, metadata:dict}
   resp {text:str, structured:dict|null, provider:str, model:str, usage:{prompt_tokens:int,completion_tokens:int,total_tokens:int}, latency_ms:int}
   Provider chosen by Settings.llm_provider; breaker.CircuitBreaker degrades to Settings.llm_fallback_provider ('mock') on timeout/error/open circuit. With LLM_PROVIDER=gemini and NO ADC creds the Gemini SDK import/client build raises lazily at call time -> breaker returns MockAdapter response (provider:'mock', structured {rationale, evidence}) with HTTP 200, so stack runs credential-free (docs/04 §4). providers/base.py defines LLMProvider Protocol + LLMRequest/LLMResponse/TokenUsage/ProviderHealth dataclasses. google-genai==1.0.0 is an OPTIONAL extra [project.optional-dependencies].gemini (lazy-imported, not installed by default); build Gemini image with `uv sync ... --extra gemini`. trace_id read from metadata.trace_id.

4) decision-engine  POST /v1/decide
   req  {transaction_id:str, verdicts:dict[AgentName,Verdict], candidate_routes:[CandidateRoute], trace_id?:str}
        (AgentName keys: 'risk','fraud','routing','policy','merchant','checkout_personalization'; a missing agent is simply absent from the map.)
   resp = acip_common.schemas.DecisionRenderedPayload {decision, composite_score, strategy='weighted_veto', route, route_alternatives[], recommended_method, contributing_verdicts[], explanation, degraded_agents[]}
   aggregator.aggregate(verdicts, candidate_routes, settings) is PURE (docs/02 §5): (1) hard veto = policy DECLINE OR fraud.score>=fraud_block_threshold -> DECLINE; (2) composite=w_risk*risk+w_fraud*fraud banded by approve_max/challenge_max; (3) routing overlay = candidate_routes ranked by success_rate (top route + alternatives) on non-DECLINE; (4) merchant soft constraint = Verdict with decision_hint CHALLENGE or an Evidence(signal='force_challenge', value>=1.0) upgrades APPROVE->CHALLENGE; (5) checkout_personalization advisory only -> recommended_method taken from that verdict's rationale, never changes decision. Missing risk OR fraud -> Settings.missing_risk_fraud_policy (default CHALLENGE; zero-verdict case returns CHALLENGE). ALL thresholds/weights from Settings. ORCHESTRATOR (FEAT-003): build the verdicts map keyed by AgentName, pass candidate_routes from the shared representation; recommended_method is surfaced from personalization.rationale (set that agent's Verdict.rationale to the method name).
